// endpoint_set_workspace_hidden.proto — SetWorkspaceHidden: move a workspace
// into the sidebar's HIDDEN WORKSPACES section, or back out of it. SIDEBAR
// section.
//
// A HIDDEN WORKSPACE'S CACHE IS LEFT TO LAPSE. Its worktree and its place in
// the registry are kept; the roster resolver hoists its row out of every
// grouping into frontend.v1.WorkspaceRoster.hidden, and the Emacs tab bar
// stops drawing, numbering and navigating to its tab, exactly as it does for a
// workspace whose repository section is collapsed. Its session's keep-alives
// are HELD (shim.v1.SetKeepalive, 2026-10-13), so its prompt cache lapses on
// its own clock, and the hidden row counts down to that moment
// (frontend.v1.RosterRowWhenHiddenCache). When it comes, the session is stood
// down as the idle sweep stands one down (it sleeps, and its conversation is
// kept), never under a running turn. SHOWING it again before then runs the
// keep-alives again; showing it starts nothing by itself either way: the
// editor asks for it with OpenTabs, which brings it up and answers when it is
// open. The new state arrives on the roster stream.
//
// DURABLE: the daemon records the flag on the workspace, so a hidden
// workspace stays hidden across a daemon restart.

